---
// D-33 manifest probe — the PUBLIC set.
//
// One import. That is the whole point of D-33: a page names its surface, not
// its component sheets, and the manifest is the single place the sheet list
// lives. Adding a component to this page without adding its sheet to the
// manifest renders it visibly unstyled, which is the accepted and deliberately
// loud failure mode.
//
// This page exists so `manifest.css` is exercised by a real build rather than
// only by greps, and so `check-css-size.mjs` has a public-surface route to
// measure. Plans 09-11 replace it with the real public sketches; the manifest
// they import is this one.
//
// No hydration directive anywhere below, so this route ships zero framework JS
// and stays inside `check-no-js.sh`'s protection rather than its exclusion
// list. The components rendered are the hook-free set already proven safe by
// probe/static.astro.
//
// Dark by default (DSGN-03) — the public site's mode, and the one where the
// charcoal cascade is actually contested.

import { Card, Chip, Heading, Text } from "@akhil-saxena/design-system";

import "../../styles/manifest.css";
---

<html lang="en" class="dark" data-brand="charcoal">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>probe/manifest-public — D-33 public manifest</title>
	</head>
	<body style="background: var(--cream); color: var(--ink); margin: 0;">
		<main style="padding: 2rem; display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; max-width: 60rem;">
			<Heading level={1}>Public manifest</Heading>
			<Text>
				One import line pulls the token layer, the charcoal faces, the charcoal
				tokens, base, and thirteen per-component sheets — in that order, in one
				file, so nothing can reorder them.
			</Text>
			<div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem;">
				<Chip tone="default">architecture</Chip>
				<Chip tone="default">nature</Chip>
			</div>
			<Card>
				<Heading level={2}>The measurement</Heading>
				<Text>
					`node check-css-size.mjs` reports what this route actually ships, linked
					and inlined, raw and gzip.
				</Text>
			</Card>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
